WEBVTT

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.490
This is reckless, Princess.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.400
Won't you consider resting for a bit?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.210
I'm all right.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:18.930
If we don't make haste, we will fall further behind the others.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.680
B-But...

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.290
We can rest at that oasis.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.680
Princess!

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.100
I don't see why you want to join those people...

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.820
I feel like I've been revived.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.430
Far too carefree...

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:50.650
We've no idea where within this desert those people have fled!

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.820
That's true, but...

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.330
Did you just call me?

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.320
No.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.340
I'm certain I heard...

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.920
Princess, a moment!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.330
I haven't finished speaking to you!

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.070
Princess!

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.460
You didn't notice, Jiiya?

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.670
That manas, overflowing with the aura of life?

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.670
Manas? Well...

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.710
I wish to know more about them.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:30.770
Just now, that...

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.200
A town, <i>there</i>?!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.990
Princess, please stop!

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:46.710
That is a state-of-the-art Bigfoot ordered secretly by the Kingdom for your personal use!

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.740
Princess!

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.770
PATH OF TRUTH

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.200
Princess, Princess!

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.530
Yes?

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.150
Please, give up on the idea!

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.080
There are a number of fellows here I don't like the look of.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.160
This is no place for an heiress to the throne to step foot in.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.670
Coming this far won't hurt.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.820
Hey, look at that!

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.360
Watch out! Run!

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.650
Huh?

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.460
What is it?

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.640
Bigfoots running amuck!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.630
See, I knew it!

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.340
S-Save us!

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.820
Hey, wait up! Hey!

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.220
They ran away from us again.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.560
Knock it off, will you?!

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.150
{bg}Pardon?

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.990
Sheesh. They should try putting themselves in our shoes and having to <i>find</i> opponents for them.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.540
Don't act stupid!

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.730
Cut it out, you guys!

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.520
This is a place I'd hate to give up our chance with, though...

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.090
Oh, no...

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.500
Ganz, get over here a sec!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.100
All right! Come down already!

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.130
Man, this needs replacing too?

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.290
Desert-grade parts are not cheap, so go easy!

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.070
We'll certainly be careful from now on, right,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:24.830
Dan?

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:25.800
Look who's talking!

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.490
No wait, isn't this <i>your</i> fault?!

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.710
No mistakin' it, that's him...

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:28.970
Pardon?

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.560
"Pardon" my ass?! Are you even listening?!

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.560
...Iceman Hotty!

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.200
It looks like he's only passed out.

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.850
Ganz, you shall carry him to the trailer.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.480
All right, retreat!

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.940
Princess...

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.400
How many times does this make it?

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.990
We're not here for pro wrestling!

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.010
Pardon?

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.710
Take that "Pardon" and shove it!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.520
Destroy!

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.540
You did it then...

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.050
...and then...

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.580
Destroy!

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.960
...and then!

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:08.920
You destroy the opponents and it doesn't even come close to a match!

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.220
And worse, you did it then,

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.650
and then, and then,

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:12.600
and then!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.600
Why do you lob them at me too?!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.010
Don't mind that.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.310
One day you'll catch up to me.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:22.520
If this goes on and no one ever wants to play us, what're you gonna do about it?!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:25.720
Dan.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.160
Yeah? Did I finally get through your thick skull?

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.320
Do people dislike you that much?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:39.100
My... My legendary right hand wants to wring your neck so bad!

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.240
Your luck with men remains awful.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.300
It's okay.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.510
If I want to get out, I can do it whenever I want.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.930
Uh-huh... uh-huh... really?

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.020
Who is this guy?

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.420
It seems like he came over the desert chasing after us.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.970
What?! Again?

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.900
How is he?

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.680
No external injuries.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.510
He's just unconscious.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.090
I'm sure he'll wake up soon.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.350
Good!

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:09.270
If he'd been hurt bad, we'd have to take responsibility.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:12.580
You're a worrywart like always.

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.850
This kid...

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:20.060
I'm sure I remember him in the Open City Basketball second round match...

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.040
His name was, uh...

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:21.930
Yo, yo.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.170
So how's the kid you picked up?

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:25.040
I'm sure it was...

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.420
No. 68, Allan Naismith.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.480
Huh?! Where am I?

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.200
Oh, he's alive!

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:34.900
Mr. Dan!

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.390
"Mr. Dan"?

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.900
I've finally met you!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:46.270
So you were searching for us this whole time?

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:49.240
Yes. I wanted to join Mr. Dan's companions, no matter what!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:54.120
If he's that starry-eyed about you, then there's no way you can refuse, is there, "Mr. Dan"?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.580
Who are you calling "Mr. Dan"?!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.940
It doesn't make me happy if a <i>guy's</i> starry-eyed for me!

00:05:57.940 --> 00:05:59.620
Oh, Mr. Dan!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:03.750
How could you make eyes at other men, you wretch, when you have me?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.290
Can the "Mr. Dan" crap, you creep!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.640
I'll do the very best I can!

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.130
So please accept me, Mr. Dan!

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.220
Quit calling me that!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.510
It's because you keep calling me "Mr. Dan" that everyone thinks it's funny and copies you!

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.240
I'm sorry, Mr. Dan.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:17.590
I just told you to quit calling me that!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.850
That group behind us has been making a racket for a while.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:19.890
Shall we leave?

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:20.860
Yeah, guess so.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.690
...and here of all places!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:24.660
What's wrong with that?

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.260
He's asking so nicely.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:27.280
Don't joke around!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.730
You think the group can stand adding more useless baggage?

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.770
C'mon, let's go!

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.930
It's enough just having jackasses like Iceman!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.750
Right? What the hell, he's gone!

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.580
Where'd that jerk get to?

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:41.050
If you're asking about Iceman, he said earlier he was gonna take a look around because the moon was pretty.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.710
Just <i>look</i> at how much that guy disrupts the group.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.880
I'll go look for him!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.780
Hey! Don't just leave in the middle of conversations!

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.650
What's your problem?

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:52.830
You like him, don't you, "Mr. Dan"?

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:53.970
I <i>told</i> you...

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:59.060
Mr. Iceman! Mr. Iceman!

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.170
I wonder how far he went?

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.820
You can see the moon just fine from here...

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:09.830
Who's there?

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.860
Princess!

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:19.200
You're unscathed!

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.810
Jiiya!

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.210
Try calling me again.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.320
Pardon? Princess.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.040
That's not it.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.000
Jiiya, you can't hear anything?

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:32.170
Maybe...

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:34.990
I heard it!

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.770
A very suspicious noise indeed!

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:37.720
Wait, Jiiya!

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:44.900
What could they be doing?

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.430
Hark! Thieves!

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.600
Alert, alert!

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.040
Jiiya, shhhh!

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.820
Iceman and that kid are sure taking their sweet time.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.590
You worried about them, Dan?

00:07:58.590 --> 00:07:59.430
As if!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.830
Jeez, why do I have to put up with this stuff?

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.120
Good nap.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.050
Got any food?

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.210
All you've done is sleep, so why—

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:11.680
Oh, food!

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:12.300
Hey!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.840
Why are you chasing me?

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.430
We can't just...

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.430
...let someone go...

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.200
...who's seen what we were doing!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.430
I'm telling you, I didn't see anything!

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.810
I, Jiiya shall face you!

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.320
Three men against a kid?

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:39.670
This boorish bunch hardly suits a night with such a beautiful moon.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:40.760
Y-You're—

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:41.460
Iceman!

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:42.150
What?!

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:47.800
Oh! Could it be you're Captain Barkas, with Doni and Sarem?

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:48.900
Have you been well?

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.520
"Been well"? Why, you—

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.220
Chewy... lizards...

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:56.510
Spanky! You're eating something again?

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.830
What are you guys doing here?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:00.900
Mr. Dan!

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:04.220
Yes, during my evening jog I ran into some people I never expected to see.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.870
What? You know them?

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:11.740
Captain Barkas, Doni, and Sarem, from my former team.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.570
Crap. More people gathering.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.140
Former teammates?

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:21.660
If you are, why don't you look too happy to see each other?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.030
Come to think of it, I heard that you quit playing and went back home,

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.010
so this town must be where you grew up.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.330
But why was it again that you quit?

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.860
Because of these injuries...

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.410
...we couldn't play plain basketball any more!

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.050
We gave you your break, and how'd you repay us?

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:44.140
Backstabber!

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:47.270
I see. You're more of Destroy's victims.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.210
Calm yourselves.

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:52.720
You can force the blame for the loss of your dream onto someone else,

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:54.610
but doesn't that just make you feel empty inside?

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.610
But you are 100 percent at fault!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.780
Oh! But that makes it perfect!

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.930
Why not settle it with a match?

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:02.530
What?

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.430
Oh, I get it! Nice one!

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.580
Yeah! We were just looking for a team to play against anyway!

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:10.690
You gentlemen play as well, correct?

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.380
Basquash.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.750
You can't fool my eyes.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:15.890
I see.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:18.660
In a match we can get our payback in front of everybody!

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.470
We'll mess you up so bad you'll never operate a Bigfoot again!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.200
It appears I have no recourse.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.260
If you all feel so strongly about it.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:28.850
Then it's decided.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.730
Yeah! You'll never beat—

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.480
We have indeed accepted your challenge.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.230
Let's be sure to beat them, Dan.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.910
H-His shades?

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.910
O-Okay.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:50.990
Rouge!

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.000
Come on, Rouge!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.680
What?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.420
Man, what a lot of noise.

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:04.280
After all the trouble we went to sneaking down here for a vacation...

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.510
They say Bigfoots are gonna play a match!

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.260
Bigfoots?

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.860
Hey, didn't we see those kids in the restaurant yesterday?

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.080
Oh, that's right!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:23.740
But I have the feeling I've seen them somewhere before then...

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.710
They're the team who rampaged through Rollingtown and had to flee!

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:29.280
It was on TV!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.460
Ohhh...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.370
Let's go see.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.530
Let's, let's!

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:33.620
Hey, wait!

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:37.010
Step right up, just 300 rollings per person!

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:39.320
Children are half-price!

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.240
Allan, hand me that part?

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:41.750
Here.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.450
Thank you.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.920
Mr. Dan's team will win for sure, right?

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:47.110
Who knows...

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:48.920
It's been quite a while since they've played a decent match.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.850
And our opponents are Iceman's former teammates.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.560
They might be pretty good.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:56.850
You're prepared for whatever happens?

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:01.440
We'll make it so you'll never play normal basketball again either, Iceman.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.490
Let's make it a clean match.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.480
Right, Dan?

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.530
Stop saying it like that! {working around honorifics, FUCK YEAH!}

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.350
Come to think of it, you were pretty picky about this one, weren't you?

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:11.450
You said you'd hate to give up on having a match in this town.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.460
Of course.

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:17.390
To bloom a beautiful rose, all sort of things need to go into it.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:18.870
Huh?

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.800
Meaning that the other team is not the only thing they must contend with.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.700
Just now, that was...

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.270
All right, both teams are prepared?

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.000
The basket is there!

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.130
The whole vastness of this desert is the court!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:52.660
Gotcha!

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.040
Idiot, what are you doing?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:58.870
Gotcha!

00:12:58.870 --> 00:12:59.710
Shit!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.610
That bastard...

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:08.300
You're worthless!

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:09.540
What are you doing?

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:14.470
Whoopsy-daisie!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:16.790
I see.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.020
This ought to shape into a fun game.

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:21.980
Why you—

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:28.290
Uh-oh. What's gotten into them?

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.060
How're they doing it?

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.660
They wearing shoes that float on the sand or something?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.700
It's <i>way</i> too hard to run in this...

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:40.620
I heard that you quit playing and went back home...

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:41.540
...back home...

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:42.940
I get it!

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.120
That's right.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:46.210
This desert...

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:47.490
...is our...

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:48.950
...home court!

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:49.670
Shut up!

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:51.840
Who cares if you're a gnome short!

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.890
Doni! Here!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:13:59.890
Iceman!

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:01.140
Yes!

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:01.950
All right!

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.600
Thanks just now for that!

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.400
Pass it!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:09.920
There he goes!

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.060
Destroy.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:11.960
Mr. Dan!

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:13.160
Ouch...

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.560
Owww.... You bastard,

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:25.590
how many times do I have to tell you, Iceman?!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.160
Don't throw Destroy balls at your teammates!

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:32.800
Destroy, destroy, destroy, destroy, destroy!

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.940
That Destroy player is so wild and cool!

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:37.380
It's called "savagery."

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:41.600
I suppose this is what to expect from people on the ground.

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:42.930
Iceman!

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:46.560
What you're playing isn't basketball!

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:47.690
Basketball is...

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.070
Hey, wait a sec!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.570
...played like <i>this</i>!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.810
Oh man, this is hopeless.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.860
Maybe it is too much for them...

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.660
Sela, stick with him!

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:07.170
You little—

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:23.970
Uh-oh, that's bad.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.710
All right, this time we've got you for sure!

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:27.800
Yeah right!

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:30.550
What're you up to, Iceman?

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:31.600
Pass it already!

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.510
Stupid! It won't be a pass coming at you,

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:34.560
it'll be a Destroy ball!

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:38.450
You know, even Iceman wouldn't give up a chance at a pass with things perfectly lined up like this—

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:39.490
Incoming!

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.160
Huh?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.830
Oh, Sela too.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:55.260
You haven't changed at all, Iceman.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:59.500
All your play does is hurt your own side.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:03.120
It's because of it that no matter how long you wait, you'll always be alone.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:09.330
Didn't that Destroy stuff get you thrown out of your team before us, too?

00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:22.410
We took you in when you were all alone, and how did you repay us?

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.920
You get it, Iceman?!

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:29.470
Someone like you, who's only thinking of <i>destroying</i> the players,

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.370
has no right to play basketball!

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:31.970
Exactly!

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.050
He's so right!

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:35.210
You've got no right to play basketball!

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:35.870
Yeah!

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.780
If you don't cut it out, I'm gonna eat you!

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.620
Hey! I'm talking right now!

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:40.370
Shut up!

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:42.580
My talking comes first!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:46.000
All right, if it's come to this, we'll have a plain basketball showdown and leave out Destroy!

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.390
Get your ass out here, Iceman!

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:50.300
You <i>really</i> have no luck with men.

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.760
Don't tell me.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.520
Lately I've really been wondering about that.

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:54.890
Deary deary.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:56.360
What's Dan doing?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.940
Looks like he's giving Iceman a piece of his mind.

00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:00.550
Well, and no wonder.

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:04.280
Iceman's Destroy balls are keeping it from being a real game.

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:06.460
They really are still children.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:10.120
What you with your eyes isn't always the complete truth.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:13.560
Hey, you listening, Iceman?!

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.180
You listening, ice-man?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.570
'Cause if you're gonna do your silent thing and ignore us, I've got an idea of my own!

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:21.810
Yeah, blink and miss it, the stupid-head says he's got an idea!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:22.300
Listen!

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:24.610
That's right! Listen good!

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:25.850
This is it!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:28.510
You're finished!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.120
Is that all?!

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:36.130
T-This is it...

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.190
You're...

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:40.320
This is it, you're finished.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:41.800
You're finished...

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:53.750
He's kind of nuts!

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:55.290
Awesome!

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:58.690
Well, this isn't a game at all now.

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:01.330
Think maybe we should run away too?

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.470
Destroy, destroy, destroy, destroy!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.000
We're gonna die, die, die, die!

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:06.250
That idiot!

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.700
Has Iceman gotten worse than he was before?!

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:09.270
Yeah!

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.270
Dunk Mask, give up already!

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:13.150
Dan, you should run!

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.860
Yeah, get out of here, stupid-head!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.350
Run?

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.480
You're kidding.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:20.320
There's no way I'm running!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.500
I can't afford to run!

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.550
Destroy, destroy!

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.330
Dan!

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:33.710
Iceman's gonna throw his true Destroy...

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.640
Destroy!

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:38.210
...and I'm gonna take that sucker straight on!

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.500
That area's...

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:48.010
Oh crap!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.570
He stopped it.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.940
He did it! He caught a Destroy ball...

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.810
How's that?! I took it, Iceman!

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:10.870
Say your prayers...

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:13.290
Huh?

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:14.720
Dan.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:16.630
Nice catch.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.670
Y-You don't mean...

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:22.090
Could it be...

00:19:22.090 --> 00:19:23.130
...every time up until now...

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.470
That, and that, and those, and all of them...

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.050
They were <i>all</i>...

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:29.890
...passes?

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:31.810
Thought so.

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:35.190
You... are hard to understand!

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.290
Dan, run! The basket!

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:41.080
The Destroy cleared off the sand and made a path!

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.030
Okay!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.830
Go, Mr. Dan!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:47.630
Huh? What are those three doing?

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:53.210
Come to think of it, the other night...

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.960
That voice again.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:04.310
Basquash!

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:09.450
W-Wait a sec! What is this?!

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:13.600
"Three-Man Team of Tomb Raiders Captured," and it's these three?

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:18.010
"Before dawn this morning, three men, who appeared to be engaged in grave robbing,

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:21.830
were taken into custody near the desert city of Float Town."

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:28.850
"Because of their suspicious testimony—that they have 'seen God', that we are 'all done for,' and so on—

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:30.470
they were transferred to a psychiatric ward, and scheduled for questioning soon."

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.030
The hell?

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:34.780
Then they weren't sportsmen at all.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:36.200
Right, Iceman?

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:40.360
Barkas and the others must have had their own reasons for what they did after they quit basketball.

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:44.840
And no matter who they are, everyone has a surface and an underside, Dan.

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:56.100
The voice is getting distant.

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:16.090
I'm sick of this sand and dust everywhere.

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:17.920
The next town will have plenty of distractions.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.140
Let's sweat it out.

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:21.460
Really? Don't promise more than you can deliver.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.430
Next time, Idol Attack!

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:27.430
NEXT TIME

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:27.430
IDOL

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:27.430
ATTACK!

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:25.170
Underestimate them and you'll regret it!
